# Shell scripts must stay LF. A CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/sh\r`) fails to exec inside
# Linux containers with "no such file or directory", which breaks
# docker-entrypoint.sh and therefore every container command
# (migrate / server / worker / app). Enforce LF regardless of the committer's
# platform or core.autocrlf setting so the image is always buildable.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
